{"kind":"request","text":"Review and incorporate: use cases, pointing at things and claims of agreement.\n\nBranch planner/use-cases-pointing-20261027, head 18103d2b311ee557c0fb368027d52762e51c53ef, base main 6f47bf98fa09ac0f3957ac9f6cc3ae21b2333b1e, pushed. One path: docs/use-cases.md. Documentation only. The doc-links check passes (713 links, 0 broken) and the commit-message check passes.\n\nDirection (Hugh, 2026-10-27): read with Star and Griesemer's boundary objects, Appleton's \"Planning with Agents\" and Licklider's externalized models, the use-case cards overfit onto assumed requirements of specific actors. The things in the cases are concrete, and their significance is nebulous. Overfit happens where a card or a package forces a thing into the structured realm without consensus. A dap room must support both pointing at things and claims of consensus.\n\nWhat the head adds:\n1. A new first section under \"What the cases have in common\": \"Pointing at things, and claims of agreement\". Two acts that no application defines (pointing; a claim of agreement by named parties); the rule that an application's structure is entered only through a claim by the parties it binds or through an authority one party already holds; three degrees of agreement (the same thing, the same rules, the same conclusion); and how a matter moves a fact up and down those degrees.\n2. One paragraph in the introduction: a card's cast, decision rights and closing are one telling, not requirements.\n3. Two sentences in \"Three kinds of statement\": own statements and documents are pointing; a signed act is a claim by one party; a claim of agreement is a signed act by several.\n4. \"What a reusable application needs to say\" split into what the application fixes for every member and what it leaves to each party. An item's final state ends the item and closes no party's part.\n5. The Source section cites the five sources.\nNo card was changed. The \"Who decides\" lines stay as the example telling.\n\nAsked of the planner: file a checker review at this head; revise for findings with child commits on the branch; land as a planner head. The companion proposal for the package structure is on branch planner/pointing-claims-packages-20261027, filed as its own request on the same date. The two heads do not link to each other. Add a cross-link from \"What a reusable application needs to say\" to the note once both have landed.","body":{"conditions":"docs/use-cases.md on main carries the pointing-and-claims section, the split list and the source citations after checker approval; the doc-links check passes at the landing head.","target":"inherit","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}